    "description": "Reviewer briefing and reading plans (D7)\n\n## Summary\n\nThis PR gives the reviewers the briefing and the reading procedure of D7. It closes #20 and #25. D6 already put the PR title, labels and body in the description block.\n\n- The reviewer user message holds a `changed_files` block before the diff. A deleted file has its own line, because the head checkout has no file to read.\n- Gather records the changed files that the change deletes.\n- diff-bugs, history, tests and security each have a reading plan in numbered steps. Each plan starts with the changed files in full, then reads the callers and callees, then the tests that cover the changed behaviour. The history plan matches the blame lines of prior fixes against the diff. The security plan follows each outside input to its uses and reads the checks that guard each changed handler.\n- conventions, docs-and-comments and description-drift get no read-in-full step. They work from the diff and read files only when they need context.\n- The design (section 3.4) and TICKETS.md record the change.\n\n## Eval\n\nOne repeat on the pinned cases (`e6ddf81`) against the 0.5.0 baseline. The gate passed.\n\n| Metric | Baseline 0.5.0 | This PR |\n|---|---|---|\n| Recall | 0.396 | 0.431 |\n| Precision | 0.722 | 0.818 |\n| Adjudicated precision | n/a | 0.939 |\n| Raw recall | n/a | 0.616 |\n| Cost per PR | $4.65 | $6.03 |\n\n| Case | Raw recall | Recall | Precision | Posted | Cost |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| martian-calcom-8330 | 0.714 | 0.571 | 0.667 | 6 | $11.23 |\n| martian-discourse-graphite-1 | 1.000 | 0.625 | 0.833 | 6 | $14.29 |\n| martian-sentry-93824 | 0.889 | 0.778 | 1.000 | 7 | $7.90 |\n| martian-sentry-greptile-1 | 0.889 | 0.667 | 0.750 | 8 | $11.65 |\n| reviewbench-axios-10836 | 1.000 | 0.500 | 1.000 | 1 | $1.40 |\n| reviewbench-claire-de-binare-1550 | 0.000 | 0.000 | - | 0 | $3.44 |\n| reviewbench-disaster-ninja-fe-1166 | 1.000 | 0.667 | 0.667 | 3 | $3.70 |\n| reviewbench-ensnode-1938 | 0.000 | 0.000 | - | 0 | $0.74 |\n| reviewbench-flatten-js-244 | 0.333 | 0.167 | 1.000 | 1 | $2.99 |\n| reviewbench-statswales-frontend-626 | 0.333 | 0.333 | 1.000 | 1 | $2.91 |\n\nCost per PR rose by 30%. One repeat gives no spread, so the gains in recall and precision can be noise. The baseline has no raw recall to compare with.\n\nThis eval ran before the last commit. In that run, every reviewer got the read-in-full instruction. conventions, docs-and-comments and description-drift cost $7.37 over ten cases against $3.28 before D7. A later commit removes the instruction from those three. Its eval at one repeat on the same pin:\n\n| Metric | Baseline 0.5.0 | All seven read in full | Four read in full |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Recall | 0.396 | 0.431 | 0.438 |\n| Raw recall | n/a | 0.616 | 0.568 |\n| Precision | 0.722 | 0.818 | 0.714 |\n| Adjudicated precision | n/a | 0.939 | 0.786 |\n| Cost per PR | $4.65 | $6.03 | $5.00 |\n| Cost of the three reviewers | n/a | $7.37 | $3.32 |\n\nThe gate passed. The precision drop comes mostly from sentry-greptile. There, four posted findings state one defect on the same line, and the merge did not join them. Six extras judge queries also gave no answer, so adjudicated precision is a floor. TICKETS.md lists the merge miss as a follow-up. The cost of the four deep reviewers also fell between the two runs, from $13.20 to $10.43, with the same prompts for three of them, so one repeat carries a lot of noise.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] `npm test`, `npm run lint`, `npm run typecheck` and `npm run build` pass.\n- [x] The eval runs at one repeat on the pinned cases and the gate passes.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01XrBTZfeb8Fxs7Pynw8RhjV\n",
